{"title":"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems#Problem_19\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Problems\">2021 AMC 10B #19</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems#Problem_12\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems\">2021 AMC 12B #12</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_Alternative_Ending\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 Alternative Ending</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(System_of_equations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (System of equations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a finite set of positive integers. If the greatest integer in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is removed from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, then the average value (arithmetic mean) of the integers remaining is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If the least integer in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is also removed, then the average value of the integers remaining is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If the greatest integer is then returned to the set, the average value of the integers rises to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The greatest integer in the original set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> greater than the least integer in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. What is the average value of all the integers in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f70efd93527dc889ea7428b3db70c8b6b67bdb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }36.2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }36.4 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }36.6\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }36.8 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"455\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can then say that \\( \\frac{A+S(n)}{n+1} = 32 \\), \\( \\frac{S(n)}{n} = 35 \\), and \\( \\frac{B+S(n)}{n+1} = 40 \\). \n</p><p>Expanding gives us \\( A+S(n) = 32n+32 \\), \\( S(n) = 35n \\), and \\( B+S(n) = 40n+40 \\). \n</p><p>Substituting \\( S(n) = 35n \\) to all gives us \\( A+35n=32n+32 \\) and \\( B+35n=40n+40 \\). \n</p><p>Solving for \\( A \\) and \\( B \\) gives \\( A=-3n+32 \\) and \\( B = 5n+40 \\). \n</p><p>We now need to find \\( \\frac{S(n)+A+B}{n+2} \\). We substitute everything to get \\( \\frac{35n+(-3n+32)+(5n+40)}{n+2} \\), or \\( \\frac{37n+72}{n+2} \\). \n</p><p>Say that the answer to this is \\( Z \\). Then, \\( Z \\) needs to be a number that makes \\( n \\) a positive integer. The only options that work is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de48c6bb6c5fb7c902e0230af3ad546359c783e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }36.6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c874f8f03a77c10f663b3e2ebbc303d944507a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }36.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>However, if 36.6 is an option, we get \\( n=3 \\). So that means that \\(A\\) is \\(23\\) and \\(B\\) is \\(55\\), and \\( S(n)=105 \\). But if there is \\(3\\) terms, then the middle number is \\(105\\), but we said that \\( B \\) is the largest number in the set, so therefore our answer cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de48c6bb6c5fb7c902e0230af3ad546359c783e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }36.6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" /> and is instead <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c874f8f03a77c10f663b3e2ebbc303d944507a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }36.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"30\" /> and now, we're finished!\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_Alternative_Ending\">Solution 1 Alternative Ending</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 Alternative Ending\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If A is smaller than B by 72 therefore from the equation on the top you can find out that \\(N = 8\\) using substitution the plug it in to the equation \\( \\frac{37n+72}{n+2} \\) then you will get that Z = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c874f8f03a77c10f663b3e2ebbc303d944507a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }36.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>This was more efficient then the last part.\n</p><p>~LittleWavelet\n</p><p>~Pinotation (Grammar and Formatting)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the lowest value be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and the highest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let the sum be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> and the amount of numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/739ec2fe12cbde0881a8d7424ef485069fa5c93b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Z-G}{n-1}=32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a189db6918996382ce55d3f0b03d9df95d67e2ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Z-L-G}{n-2}=35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"133\" height=\"41\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3fa90fe452f83bf96d021c96a81eea4090d5487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Z-L}{n-1}=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546f2047f5447edd5c12d0f18ccad0a6d85d003d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G=L+72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. Clearing denominators gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f564dd7b0237624a500b1135c22876d6135615b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z-G=32n-32$\" width=\"143\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad3f374b8eb7587f7cde7ffa29ca79fb9b9be54b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z-L-G=35n-70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc23102b684ac7202cd9a00bfa92db67fc8593b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z-L=40n-40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"16\" />. We use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546f2047f5447edd5c12d0f18ccad0a6d85d003d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G=L+72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> to turn the first equation into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87183d5c065168e1de231b1ab1a9b1098cf32c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z-L=32n+40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131b26ff9de68192808515699f927199ff9d227f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z-L=40(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" /> we substitute it into the equation which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1b21210db29332b1a7d9ce088fd457f23aeee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. Turning the second into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f86869be0a880409057cdc2a223f58924264f109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z-2L=35n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"14\" /> using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546f2047f5447edd5c12d0f18ccad0a6d85d003d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G=L+72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61fc4c58331cd3570e13aa7e0416fd6df5acc47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L=8$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d900775b7d7158079c1c1da3aa4baa7648e322d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z=368$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> so the average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdba479047f39eacc9ce67ca73d7e59a33a472b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Z}{n}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }36.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"39\" /> ~aop2014\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the greatest integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the smallest, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the sum of the numbers in S excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of elements in S.\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa2eb7aa98178a74a0b205e11561667e59baf97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>First, when the greatest integer is removed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c790342658146aaf1a93abf16821c7d97ad582b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S-x}{k-1}=32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>When the smallest integer is also removed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40b4b84247d2724862abe71b148648606a5cbe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S-x-y}{k-2}=35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>When the greatest integer is added back, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae20812c8fe38afb0fb9c75842e3d510d4b2e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S-y}{k-1}=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7100961f9f3c39b8a64793f0af32baa76be96fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y+72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nAfter you substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7100961f9f3c39b8a64793f0af32baa76be96fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y+72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />, you have 3 equations with 3 unknowns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2e8e8dd78b26ddc9ac278cc179101d30644cae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3bc4fd393da616626868cd212417004b07848a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S-y-72=32k-32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/8748c05dc156245d6f03952f1a207386deed434d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S-2y-72=35k-70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1e636fbadf56fd3e0032130a431c39d5c98e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S-y=40k-40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>This can be easily solved to yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afd9b066c6c1fb6ef4383cb93bbabe6521c36d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4808fab877e290bdc0e68ce61cc8a852fd397b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec88bb150f9c2f6da0b68982ee1984b55409948f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=368$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a63588d48cc9015ddcfc1560cf86e98b33b51972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> average value of all integers in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0ed7a840e6619394952f139a2b1e77eac66453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=S/k = 368/10 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }36.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"234\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ SoySoy4444\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We should plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf347491b110306078dd4dd2cb37c64f3764ab17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36.2$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and assume everything is true except the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> part. We then calculate that part and end up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea67138856a9e932a93e69ec7586fa5b6bfed62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. We also see with the formulas we used with the plug in that when you increase by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a270a7be617f39b92e4821298c4555cffe496c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea67138856a9e932a93e69ec7586fa5b6bfed62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> part decreases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6ee426e2e724a4e7255dd71bdd7dbd6c75ab04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.25$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. The answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c874f8f03a77c10f663b3e2ebbc303d944507a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }36.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"30\" />. You can work backwards because it is multiple choice and you don't have to do critical thinking. ~Lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179da0ec9ea4d36881248f7f1380dacc78fc91c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{a_1, a_2, a_3, \\hdots, a_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/59948e6975ac1352f9b31405e6a3c74319803884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; a_3 &lt; \\hdots &lt; a_n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"12\" /> We are given the following: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/c/aecd91e93199e4289661420c0a40e01ad4e4587b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{\\begin{cases} \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} a_i = 32(n-1) = 32n-32, \\\\ \\sum_{i=2}^n a_i = 40(n-1) = 40n-40, \\\\ \\sum_{i=2}^{n-1} a_i = 35(n-2) = 35n-70, \\\\ a_n-a_1 = 72 \\implies a_1 + 72 = a_n. \\end{cases}}\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"96\" /> Subtracting the third equation from the sum of the first two, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/9385e377c1d9466ec465f5d7af6c38e350b5ed64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i = \\left(32n-32\\right) + \\left(40n-40\\right) - \\left(35n-70\\right) = 37n - 2.\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"47\" /> Furthermore, from the fourth equation, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1d47f0e7fcf8936f7f9dafdd35b3c433092df5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=2}^{n} a_i - \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} a_i = \\left[\\left(a_1 + 72\\right) + \\sum_{i=2}^{n-1} a_i\\right] - \\left[\\left(a_1\\right) + \\sum_{i=2}^{n-1} a_i\\right] = \\left(40n-40\\right)-\\left(32n-32\\right).\\]\" width=\"628\" height=\"53\" /> Combining like terms and simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df050ae567b006f1bcec0e63ca273e30f0e3ba55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[72 = 8n-8 \\implies 8n = 80 \\implies n=10.\\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"13\" /> Thus, the sum of the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e710db2a2946b781265c3893fa721111ee7b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37 \\cdot 10 - 2 = 368,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" /> and since there are 10 elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2e8e8dd78b26ddc9ac278cc179101d30644cae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> the average of the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c62f3f2645836939d98cc364962558443a3d553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{368}{10}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }36.8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"129\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~peace09\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd94bfe7d4ea293cb74d358753e3894e120c3c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S, m_l = 32, \\Sigma_l = m_l \\cdot (n-1), m_g = 40,  \\Sigma_g = m_g \\cdot (n-1), m_{lg} = 35,  \\Sigma_lg = m_{lg} \\cdot (n-2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"687\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6340add68b00dfd706fe14fccb1aa76d75bc2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Sigma_g - \\Sigma_l = 72 = (n-1) \\cdot (m_g - m_l) \\implies n = 1 + \\frac {72}{m_g - m_l} = 1 + \\frac {72}{40-32}=10.\\]\" width=\"580\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c29c4e47b4fe757f9cd4deadd32205e352afffd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m = \\frac {\\Sigma_g + \\Sigma_l - \\Sigma_{lg}}{n} = \\frac {40 \\cdot 9 + 32 \\cdot 9 - 35 \\cdot 8}{10} = 36.8.\\]\" width=\"405\" height=\"37\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28System_of_equations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(System_of_equations)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (System of equations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (System of equations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dRdT9gzm-Pg\">https://youtu.be/dRdT9gzm-Pg</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4iCAZRUESs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p4iCAZRUESs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FV9AnyERgJQ?t=676\">https://youtu.be/FV9AnyERgJQ?t=676</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/TbHluJQoy8s\">https://youtu.be/TbHluJQoy8s</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_.28English-Chinese_Bilingual.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MRENTHUSIASM_(English-Chinese_Bilingual)\">Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MRENTHUSIASM (English-Chinese Bilingual)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/T4361nIPzhw\">https://youtu.be/T4361nIPzhw</a>\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B\">2021 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12